            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> can we do something like\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> highlight TabLineSel guibg=bg guifg=fg ctermbg=white ctermfg=black\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> instead?\r\n\r\nThat's essentially `hi default link TabLineSel Normal`. Not particularly against this, but it does make it blend a bit too much with normal buffer. At least with bold it is usually visibly different.\r\n\r\nLinking `TabLineSel` to `StatusLine` in the default color scheme makes more sense, especially together with `TabLine` linked to `StatusLineNC`. If I remember correctly, this was my original plan during the initial rewrite, but the `StatusLine` back then was either too visible or too invisible. The 28ff4deda7a0c452d3a35de3da5e5ff676824915 made this default link more appropriate to me.",
